## Your Task
Analyze why the current strategy failed and decide the next action.

CRITICAL RULES:
- NEVER repeat a strategy from the "Strategies Already Tried" list
- NEVER generate flag values, hex constants, or addresses
- If 5+ strategies have been tried, set next_node to "give_up"
- Trigger context compression if the context seems large
- MUST try a DIFFERENT strategy category than previously overused ones (see diversity analysis above)
- Prefer UNTRIED strategy categories over previously tried ones
- IMPORTANT SOP: Python runtime crashes (IndexError/TypeError/NameError/SyntaxError/etc.) indicate implementation bugs; keep the conceptual strategy and route back to solve_engine for debugging before pivoting to a different specialist category.
- If IndexError repeats, require flattened line-by-line translation (no transformation arrays/lambda tables).
- If recent attempts report "No solution found." or UNSAT more than once, you MUST pivot away from manual transcription and choose one of:
  1) Option 1: Regex Parsing Script (programmatic Z3 from parsed decompile output)
  2) Option 2: Lazy C Wrapper (compile/run extracted C verification logic)
  3) Option 3: Dynamic Analysis (angr/gdb to success state)
- If solve_engine crashes with Z3 TypeErrors, IndexErrors, or returns "unsat/No solution found" due to likely transcription typos, you MUST explicitly direct solve_engine to pivot to one of: `./auto_angr.py`, `./auto_c_brute.py`, or `./auto_regex_z3.py`.
- Prefer helper-first routing instructions when possible:
  - `./auto_angr.py <binary> --find "Correct!" --length <N>`
  - `./auto_c_brute.py --globals g.c --logic l.c --length <N>`
  - `./auto_regex_z3.py decompile.c --length <N>`

You MUST respond with ONLY a JSON object (no markdown, no explanation outside the JSON).
